# View: <context name>

> A **Domain View** — a system slice scoped to one bounded context. Same shape as `system.md`, but partitioned. Use this when `system.md` would otherwise overflow ~500 lines, OR when a context has enough self-contained vocabulary that loading it independently of the rest is genuinely useful (progressive loading).
>
> Views are **optional**. Simple projects keep everything in `system.md`. A project with one view is fine. A project with eight is also fine. The pressure to split should come from `system.md` rotting, not from a target shape.
>
> Edits go through `lex-crystallize`, same discipline as `system.md`.

